4. Your data and your content
-----------------------------

Your data is yours. Notes stay plain files on your disk; Leonote has no
accounts and no servers that hold your notes, and the copyright holder never receives your files
and therefore cannot recover them. The encrypted backup is encrypted with
your password, which Leonote never stores or sends; if you lose it, nobody can
open that backup. Backup plans make plain zip files.

Leonote creates, edits, renames, moves, converts and deletes files in the
folders you point it at. You are responsible for keeping independent backups
of anything you cannot afford to lose.

Optional cloud storage, if it is offered and you subscribe to it, is covered
by its own terms.


5. Use of the software
----------------------

Leonote is a tool. It hosts no media and supplies no copyrighted content of
its own. What it opens or plays comes from files you provide or from addresses
you give it, requested from your computer directly from the third party
concerned. You are responsible for having the right to access that material
and for complying with the terms of the sites and services you use Leonote
with. No third-party service is guaranteed to work with Leonote or to keep
working.

Add-ons, helper programs (such as FFmpeg or whisper.cpp), AI services and
servers that you choose to install or connect are not part of Leonote: the
copyright holder does not make, check or endorse them, each comes under its own
licence and terms, and what they receive or do is between you and them.
Sections 6 and 7 apply to them in full.

External software that you run yourself, including AI agents, can read and
change your notes and tasks. Those agents are not the copyright holder's, and
the copyright holder is not responsible for anything they read, write, change,
delete or send elsewhere.

Reminders, recurring tasks and timers are conveniences and may fail to fire.
Do not rely on Leonote as the only safeguard for anything safety-critical,
medical, legal or financial.


